Sure, I know the motivation behind that, and it's certainly a valid
view. The reason why I perfer the other way is that usually I want
to write scrolls as early as necessary, that means that I don't have
those large stacks of blank (or blanked) scrolls, and if I find new
scrolls or paper golems I don't need another potion to bless those
scrolls again. (My current orcish wizard game at NAO is such a game,
BTW.) Later in the game both ways are (for me) acceptable choices.
Often I have games where I've found more than one magic marker, and I
don't bless the second one if there is no necessity, exactly to have
more options. But generally, _writing_ cursed scrolls is, in my book,
of limited use because of the reasons explained upthread.

